1
00:00:03,082 --> 00:00:06,065
Mmm, after the shower, it smells like wet earth!

2
00:00:06,115 --> 00:00:08,087
Yet tap water smells of nothing…

3
00:00:08,137 --> 00:00:10,791
So where does the smell of rain come from?

4
00:00:11,615 --> 00:00:13,021
Noah sniffs a glass of water…

5
00:00:13,071 --> 00:00:13,422
nothing!

6
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:15,329
But Mila sniffs a handful of wet soil,

7
00:00:15,379 --> 00:00:16,132
and there it is!

8
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:18,040
The smell doesn't come from the water…

9
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:19,093
but from the ground.

10
00:00:19,872 --> 00:00:21,386
Discovery mission!

11
00:00:23,915 --> 00:00:24,630
Mini mode!

12
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:28,376
In the soil live tiny bacteria that make a scent:

13
00:00:28,426 --> 00:00:28,987
geosmin.

14
00:00:29,037 --> 00:00:32,045
And plants leave oils there on dry days…

15
00:00:32,095 --> 00:00:33,930
lots of sleeping scents!

16
00:00:34,724 --> 00:00:35,272
And then,

17
00:00:35,322 --> 00:00:38,727
a drop falls on the soil and traps tiny air bubbles.

18
00:00:38,777 --> 00:00:40,455
These bubbles rise, burst…

19
00:00:40,505 --> 00:00:43,561
and shoot out a tiny mist, loaded with scents!

20
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:45,921
These scents fly up to your nose.

21
00:00:45,971 --> 00:00:47,303
And your nose is a champion:

22
00:00:47,353 --> 00:00:50,909
it can smell geosmin even when there's just one drop in a swimming pool!

23
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:55,090
After days without rain, the smell is stronger,

24
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:57,057
because the scents have piled up.

25
00:00:57,107 --> 00:00:59,023
A gentle little rain, and whoosh,

26
00:00:59,073 --> 00:01:00,145
it all flies away!

27
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:03,014
And that's why rain has a smell.

28
00:01:04,475 --> 00:01:06,232
The smell of rain comes from the soil:

29
00:01:06,282 --> 00:01:09,372
scents from bacteria and plants that the drops send into the air.

30
00:01:10,948 --> 00:01:12,780
With an adult, on a dry day:

31
00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:15,671
water a patch of soil, lean in and breathe…

32
00:01:15,721 --> 00:01:18,141
it's the smell of rain, made by you!

33
00:01:18,921 --> 00:01:20,821
And why do stars twinkle?

34
00:01:20,871 --> 00:01:22,431
The answer tomorrow.
